@using Ecnanib.DecisionEngine
@using Ecnanib.Shared
@using Ecnanib.WebUi.Pages
@using Ecnanib.WebUi.Pages.Agents

@*
    The team of an agent on the start page, as an illustration (FR-ANI-7): the four roles as the
    screen of an agent draws them, in the order that they work in and in three stages, each with
    the provider whose model fills it on a new agent and with its job. It is the pipeline of
    that screen as it is once a cycle has gone through it: every role is done, and the work was
    handed to each stage. So it is drawn by the rules of the pipeline, and reads the same in both
    themes (FR-THM-5).

    A provider is named by its name as text, to say whose model fills a role, and by nothing
    else: no logo, no picture, and no colour of its own (NFR-LEG-4). The caption says in words
    what the picture shows, so nothing relies on what moves.

    What moves is in the stylesheet alone, for a device that asks for no reduced motion and an
    account that did not reduce it (FR-ANI-4): the picture is played once, as one cycle, and
    stays as it is written here. The cards and their texts never move and are never hidden: what
    moves is the marker of a role, the second outline of a card whose role works, which is the
    empty element at the start of a card, and the line into a stage. The part says that
    something of it moves, so the script of the pages has it stand still while it is off the
    screen (FR-ANI-6). It carries no style and no script. See docs/motion.md.
*@

<figure class="team-illustration" data-moves>
    <ol class="team-pipeline">
        <li class="pipeline-stage">
            @* The two analysts work at the same time. *@
            <ul class="pipeline-parallel">
                <li>@Card(Role.MarketAnalyst)</li>
                <li>@Card(Role.SentimentAnalyst)</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li class="pipeline-stage stage-handed">@Card(Role.Strategist)</li>
        <li class="pipeline-stage stage-handed">@Card(Role.RiskManager)</li>
    </ol>

    <figcaption>@HomePages.TeamCaption</figcaption>
</figure>

@code {
    /// <summary>The name of the provider that fills each role on a new agent, as users read it.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<Role, string> Providers { get; set; } = new Dictionary<Role, string>();

    /// <summary>
    /// A role as a card: its name, whose model fills it, and its job. The card is the one of a
    /// role that is done, by the name that the stylesheet knows that by.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment Card(Role role) =>
        @<div class="pipeline-role @LivePages.ClassOf(RoleState.Done)">
            <span class="role-turn" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="role-name">@AgentPages.Describe(role).Name</span>
            <span class="role-state"><span class="role-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>@HomePages.ModelOf(Providers[role])</span>
            <span class="role-job">@AgentPages.Describe(role).Job</span>
        </div>;
}
